  "about": "How Colosseum plays generation 4's moves, abilities and evolution items, which it doesn't have. Written by hand; gen4.json is Showdown's and Pokémon Platinum's data. A new move plays as a move Colosseum has (`as`): its effect, its animation and its battle messages, with the new move's own type, power, accuracy, PP, priority, targets, effect chance and flags, as gen4.json has them from Pokémon Platinum. `exact` says whether that effect is the move's own. A move left at null has nothing close, and is left out of every learnset. An ability Colosseum lacks becomes another a Pokémon has, else the one named here. An evolution by an item Colosseum lacks becomes one by level (evolutionItems), and so does one at a place (evolutionPlaces), or one by an item the game has: Leafeon by a Leaf Stone (as generation 8 has it) for the Moss Rock, and Glaceon by levelling up holding NeverMeltIce for the Ice Rock; 0 is none.",
